WEBVTT

00:00.140 --> 00:02.263
Every Microsoft agreement starts

00:02.263 --> 00:03.722
with a set of choices.

00:03.722 --> 00:05.911
For a university, the value comes

00:05.911 --> 00:08.100
from making those choices clearly

00:08.100 --> 00:10.820
and having the right support around them.

00:11.540 --> 00:14.325
Data three brings more than thirty years

00:14.325 --> 00:15.995
of education experience,

00:15.995 --> 00:19.128
long-standing engagement with CAUDIT members,

00:19.128 --> 00:21.843
and national coverage across Australia,

00:21.843 --> 00:23.305
Fiji and the Pacific.

00:23.305 --> 00:26.438
Each institution has a local account contact,

00:26.438 --> 00:28.457
backed by Microsoft licensing

00:28.457 --> 00:30.197
and contract specialists,

00:30.197 --> 00:32.007
national solution experts,

00:32.007 --> 00:34.096
and direct escalation pathways

00:34.096 --> 00:35.140
into Microsoft.

00:35.900 --> 00:39.176
That team supports the full agreement lifecycle.

00:39.176 --> 00:42.043
It coordinates quotes, orders, enrolments,

00:42.043 --> 00:43.681
amendments and renewals.

00:43.681 --> 00:46.206
It interprets licensing requirements,

00:46.206 --> 00:48.731
provides education-specific guidance,

00:48.731 --> 00:51.734
reviews consumption and licensing positions,

00:51.734 --> 00:53.441
models renewal scenarios,

00:53.441 --> 00:55.284
and advocates for customers

00:55.284 --> 00:57.126
when licensing, entitlement

00:57.126 --> 00:59.720
or operational issues need escalation.

01:00.600 --> 01:03.260
The level of support remains flexible.

01:03.260 --> 01:06.340
Institutions with strong internal capability

01:06.340 --> 01:09.280
can focus on core licensing administration

01:09.280 --> 01:10.260
and enquiries.

01:10.260 --> 01:13.410
Those wanting deeper support can add reviews,

01:13.410 --> 01:16.140
planning, roadmap briefings, governance

01:16.140 --> 01:17.890
and specialist engagement

01:17.890 --> 01:19.360
as priorities change.

01:20.200 --> 01:23.303
My D three provides a secure central view

01:23.303 --> 01:26.632
of agreements, software and cloud reporting,

01:26.632 --> 01:29.432
quotes, orders, assets, support cases

01:29.432 --> 01:31.400
and lifecycle information.

01:32.060 --> 01:34.630
Optional Premier Support adds accountable

01:34.630 --> 01:37.200
incident ownership across Microsoft cloud

01:37.200 --> 01:38.892
and on-premises technology,

01:38.892 --> 01:41.086
using a pre-purchased pool of hours

01:41.086 --> 01:42.778
and escalation to Microsoft

01:42.778 --> 01:45.160
when product intervention is required.

01:45.940 --> 01:48.782
Around Azure, separately scoped services

01:48.782 --> 01:50.842
can provide platform support,

01:50.842 --> 01:53.968
priority incident handling, cost visibility,

01:53.968 --> 01:56.526
right-sizing, governance, monitoring

01:56.526 --> 01:58.160
and managed operations.

01:59.020 --> 02:01.615
The same relationship can connect institutions

02:01.615 --> 02:04.096
with expertise across modern work, security,

02:04.096 --> 02:05.958
data and artificial intelligence,

02:05.958 --> 02:07.537
applications and automation.

02:07.537 --> 02:09.962
Engagement can take the form of consulting,

02:09.962 --> 02:11.485
packaged services, projects

02:11.485 --> 02:13.065
or ongoing managed services.

02:13.065 --> 02:15.264
Each is scoped and purchased separately

02:15.264 --> 02:16.900
from the Microsoft agreement.

02:17.520 --> 02:20.012
University priorities change over time.

02:20.012 --> 02:21.992
Licensing optimisation may lead

02:21.992 --> 02:24.229
to cloud adoption, security uplift,

02:24.229 --> 02:27.040
responsible artificial intelligence adoption

02:27.040 --> 02:28.701
or broader transformation.

02:28.701 --> 02:31.384
Data three helps bring the right expertise

02:31.384 --> 02:33.940
into the relationship at the right time.

02:34.640 --> 02:37.552
The next agreement cycle begins

02:37.552 --> 02:41.027
by confirming scope and requirements,

02:41.027 --> 02:45.441
validating licensing and enrolment information,

02:45.441 --> 02:47.789
completing documentation,

02:47.789 --> 02:50.982
preparing onboarding and handover,

02:50.982 --> 02:53.142
then verifying licences

02:53.142 --> 02:55.960
and beginning ongoing support.

02:56.840 --> 02:59.121
Your Microsoft investment.

02:59.121 --> 02:59.998
Your way.

02:59.998 --> 03:01.840
Backed by Data three.
